      "id": 1,
      "text": "Michael Uhrich founded the settlement in 1804, and the town grew around his mill on the Tuscarawas River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.claymontlibrary.org/lochistgen",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Waterford, locals insisted on calling it Uhrich's Mill, so the name officially changed to Uhrichsville in 1839.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uhrichsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Ohio and Erie Canal and later the Pan Handle Railroad turned Uhrichsville into a bustling railroad hub in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uhrichsville%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city opened a modern water park in June 2008, adding a splash of recreation to its historic streets.",
